+# Plan — EPMCDME-5383: ZIP Upload for File Datasource
+
+## Requirements
+
+Allow users to upload a ZIP archive to a file-type datasource. The backend extracts the archive contents, stores each file individually, and makes them visible as separate entries in the datasource. The ZIP itself is not stored.
+
+Files inside the ZIP that the indexer can handle as plain text (e.g. `.md`, `.rst`) must be indexed, not silently dropped — aligned with the `PlainTextLoader` fallback behavior of direct upload.
+
+---
+
+## Tasks
+
+### Task 1 — Add `_expand_zip_file` helper to `FileDatasourceService` ✅
+
+**File**: `src/codemie/service/datasource/file_datasource_service.py`
+
+Static method that:
+- Accepts `zip_bytes: bytes`
+- Opens the archive with `zipfile.ZipFile(io.BytesIO(zip_bytes))`
+- Skips directory entries (`ZipInfo.is_dir()`)
+- Guards total uncompressed size; raises `ExtendedHTTPException(HTTP_422)` if it exceeds `_ZIP_MAX_UNCOMPRESSED_BYTES` (500 MB)
+- Derives flat filenames with `os.path.basename`
+- Skips nested ZIPs (extension == `'zip'`) with a logged warning — storing them verbatim would trigger `ZipLoader` failure at index time
+- Tracks `seen_names` to skip duplicates with a logged warning
+- Reads member bytes with `ZipFile.read(info.filename)`
+- Returns `list[tuple[str, bytes]]` — `(flat_filename, content)` pairs
+
+Extension filter: exclude only `.zip` (nested archives). Do NOT filter against `IndexKnowledgeBaseFileTypes` — the indexer accepts all unknown extensions via `PlainTextLoader` fallback, so filtering here would silently drop text files (`.md`, `.rst`, etc.) that direct upload would index correctly.
+
+**Test-first**: `test_expand_zip_file_yields_supported_files`, `test_expand_zip_file_skips_directories`, `test_expand_zip_file_skips_nested_zip`, `test_expand_zip_file_raises_on_size_bomb`, `test_expand_zip_file_skips_duplicate_filenames`
+
+---
+
+### Task 2 — Modify `upload_and_prepare_files` to expand ZIP files (UPDATE path) ✅
+
+**File**: `src/codemie/service/datasource/file_datasource_service.py`
+
+In the `for file in new_files` loop, after reading `content = file.file.read()`:
+- Check `file.filename.split(".")[-1].lower() == IndexKnowledgeBaseFileTypes.ZIP.value`
+- If ZIP: call `_expand_zip_file(content)`; iterate `(name, bytes)` pairs; `write_file` each; append to `new_paths` / `new_filenames`
+- If not ZIP: keep current behaviour (store verbatim, validate JSON if applicable)
+- ZIP filename itself is NOT added to `uploaded_files`
+
+**Test-first**: `test_upload_and_prepare_files_expands_zip`, `test_upload_and_prepare_files_zip_does_not_appear_in_uploaded_files`
+
+---
+
+### Task 3 — Apply ZIP expansion to the CREATE path in the router ✅
+
+**File**: `src/codemie/rest_api/routers/index.py`
+
+The CREATE handler `index_knowledge_base_files` (`@router.post("/index/knowledge_base/file")`) iterates files inline without going through `FileDatasourceService`. Apply the same ZIP expansion logic:
+- Add `import mimetypes` to the router imports
+- In the `for file in request.files` loop, check if extension is `zip`
+- If ZIP: call `FileDatasourceService._expand_zip_file(content)`; iterate extracted pairs; `write_file` each with `mimetypes.guess_type(name)` mime; append to `files_paths` / `uploaded_files`
+- If not ZIP: existing behaviour unchanged
+
+**Test-first**: no — this is router-level glue that mirrors already-tested service logic; the logic itself is covered by Task 1/2 tests.
+
+---
+
+### Task 4 — Align `_expand_zip_file` extension filter with indexer behaviour (pending)
+
+**File**: `src/codemie/service/datasource/file_datasource_service.py`
+
+The current implementation already drops the `IndexKnowledgeBaseFileTypes` guard (Task 1 above). This task tracks verifying the aligned behaviour with a test:
+
+- Upload a ZIP containing a `.md` file
+- Assert the extracted `.md` file IS included in the result (not skipped)
+- Confirms parity with direct-upload plain-text fallback
+
+**Test-first**: `test_expand_zip_file_includes_plain_text_files` (`.md`, `.rst`, `.log`)
+
+---
+
+## Invariants and Constraints
+
+| Constraint | Rationale |
+|---|---|
+| ZIP itself not added to `uploaded_files` | Users should see extracted files, not the archive |
+| Flat filenames (`os.path.basename`) | Keeps the datasource file list simple; avoids path separator issues across storage backends |
+| `MAX_FILE_COUNT` not enforced on extracted files | The purpose of ZIP upload is to upload more than 10 files at once |
+| Nested ZIPs skipped (not stored verbatim) | Storing them would trigger `ZipLoader`/`ZipConverter` failure at index time |
+| No extension guard beyond skipping nested ZIPs | Indexer accepts all unknown extensions via `PlainTextLoader`; guard in ZIP path would be stricter than direct upload |
+| Size guard before extraction | Prevents decompression bombs from exhausting memory |
+| `ZipLoader` in `LOADERS` dict left unchanged | Other code paths (SharePoint, direct loader use) may still pass ZIPs to it |
+| CREATE path not refactored into service | The inline router code is out of scope; ZIP expansion duplicated there for now |
+
